    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "Perfect! The bug is now fixed. Here's a summary of what was wrong and how I fixed it:\n\n## The Problem\nThe `frai gate init --ci` command through the CLI wasn't passing the `--ci` flag to the underlying `frai-gate` package, so the GitHub Actions workflow file wasn't being created.\n\n## The Root Cause\nCommander.js doesn't pass unknown options (flags like `--ci`) through the variadic arguments array when `allowUnknownOption(true)` is set. Instead, it stores them separately. The original code tried to capture arguments via the action's parameters, which didn't include these unknown flags.\n\n## The Fix\nI changed the action handler to extract the arguments directly from `process.argv` after the 'gate' command. This ensures all arguments and flags (including `--ci`) are properly passed through to the spawned `frai-gate` process:\n\n```typescript\n.action(async () => {\n  // ... setup code ...\n  const gateIndex = process.argv.indexOf('gate');\n  const args = process.argv.slice(gateIndex + 1);\n  const result = spawnSync(process.execPath, [gateCli, ...args], { stdio: 'inherit' });\n  process.exit(result.status ?? 0);\n})\n```\n\n## Verification\n\u2705 Both files are now created correctly:\n- `FRAI-SPEC.md` (the template)\n- `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` (the GitHub Actions workflow)\n\nThe workflow file contains the proper CI configuration to run the gate on every PR.",
